+The closed-form solution for the radiance $L$ observed at the camera (ray origin) from a surface hit at distance $t_{\text{hit}}$ is [S1]:
+$$ L = \exp(-\sigma_a t_{\text{hit}}) L_e $$
+Or generally, for intensity $I(s)$ at distance $s$ from an initial intensity $I_0$ [S2, book][S3, S4, unofficial]:
+$$ I(s) = I_0 \exp\left(-\int_0^s \tau(t) dt\right) $$
 The term $T(s) = \exp\left(-\int_0^s \tau(t) dt\right)$ is the transparency of the medium between $0$ and $s$ [S3, S4, unofficial].
 
